  "minutes": 10,
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "kind": "concept",
      "figure": "exp-curve-growth",
      "body": "When a coefficient sits in front, **isolate the power first**. For 3 · 2ˣ = 24: divide both sides by 3 to get 2ˣ = 8, then match bases: 8 = 2³, so x = 3. Undo the multiplication before matching."
    },
    {
      "id": "i1",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Divide, then match.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "prompt": "Solve 3 * 2^x = 24.",
        "answer": 3,
        "tolerance": 0,
        "commonErrors": [
          {
            "value": 8,
            "feedback": "8 is 2ˣ after dividing — keep going: 8 = 2³, so x = 3."
          },
          {
            "value": 21,
            "feedback": "Divide by 3, don't subtract it: 24/3 = 8 = 2³, so x = 3."
          }
        ],
        "fallbackFeedback": "24/3 = 8 = 2³, so x = 3."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "k1",
      "kind": "check",
      "body": "A base of 3.",
      "conceptTag": "exp-coeff-equation",
      "explanationVariants": [
        "Divide by 2: 54/2 = 27 = 3³, so x = 3.",
        "27 = 3³, so after dividing out the 2, x = 3."
      ],
      "widget": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "prompt": "Solve 2 * 3^x = 54.",
        "answer": 3,
        "tolerance": 0,
        "commonErrors": [
          {
            "value": 27,
            "feedback": "27 is 3ˣ after dividing — keep going: 27 = 3³, so x = 3."
          },
          {
            "value": 18,
            "feedback": "Divide by 2, not the exponent: 54/2 = 27 = 3³, so x = 3."
          }
        ],
        "fallbackFeedback": "54/2 = 27 = 3³, so x = 3."
      },
      "variant": {
        "gen": "exp-solve"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "The coefficient never becomes part of the exponent. For 5 · 2ˣ = 40: divide by 5 → 2ˣ = 8 → x = 3. The 5 only scales the output; the exponent comes from the power alone.",
      "figure": "exp-coefficient-40"
    },
    {
      "id": "i2",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Scale it away.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "prompt": "Solve 5 * 2^x = 40.",
        "answer": 3,
        "tolerance": 0,
        "commonErrors": [
          {
            "value": 8,
            "feedback": "8 is 2ˣ after dividing — finish: 8 = 2³, so x = 3."
          },
          {
            "value": 35,
            "feedback": "Divide by 5, don't subtract it: 40/5 = 8 = 2³, so x = 3."
          }
        ],
        "fallbackFeedback": "40/5 = 8 = 2³, so x = 3."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "The method is always the same: divide out the coefficient, then match bases. For 4 · 3ˣ = 36: divide by 4 → 3ˣ = 9 → x = 2.",
      "figure": "exp-divide-first"
    },
    {
      "id": "i3",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Your turn.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "prompt": "Solve 4 * 3^x = 36.",
        "answer": 2,
        "tolerance": 0,
